      "body": "`build_store` stores `memberships` for every corpus element, but it is only used during store construction and then immediately dropped. This can be a large, unnecessary memory spike (O(n·STAGES·M·depth) allocations). You can build `store` in the same pass that computes `(code, by_depth)` and still return `codes`, avoiding the extra `memberships` vector entirely.",
